WEBVTT

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.460
This time, I'll be the dealer.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.550
Best regards.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:13.340
By the way,
what cards are you living on now?

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.050
You must have a good hand.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.560
I leave that to your imagination.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.060
Case No. 10785, Inspect Relation start.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:32.820
Debate: leading candidate, Karina Komiya.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.740
Security item:
Tokyo gubernatorial election.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:41.870
Relation Block: Criminal Investigation
Department Unit One.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.210
Now, it's finally time.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.170
This will be a major turning point
for us here at Bifrost.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.590
Draw the knives
locked behind your eyelids.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.350
Reap the lives that grow into shackles.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.060
Even the lost memories that flee
once they're liberated and banished

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.020
Are an everlasting cubism.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:26.920
Cause I know that in a future gone mad,

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.590
Even nightmares are peaceful.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.710
RESET, RESET, yeah.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.590
The midnight sun
awakens and turns to a riot.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.220
A gun for a faux-friendly kiss.
A knife for a faux-revolutionary hug.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:47.440
Get rid of it all, even the frozen chains.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:51.440
Reality is always outside your head.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:56.110
In a world seen through bestial eyes,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:02.080
There is neither darkness nor light.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.790
Draw the knives
locked behind your eyelids.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.460
Reap the lives that grow into shackles.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.130
Even the false memories that flash before
your eyes impatiently and impulsively

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.800
Are an everlasting cubism.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.520
#03
Herakles and the Sirens

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.690
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.520
You have two minutes.
We can't spare any more.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.360
Do you know a man named Kojo Tsuchiya?

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.990
I don't. Will that be all?

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:44.370
Candidate Komiya is currently in the lead.
Do you have a plan to turn that around?

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.790
Ask my first secretary, Lee, about that.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:50.670
A slight disadvantage was anticipated.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:55.590
She seems to be ahead in Sibyl System's
politician suitability as well.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.170
A negligible difference.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.970
I won't deny that I'm losing.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:06.350
But I have overcome strict
daily training and many deadly struggles.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.680
My Hue will triumph in the end.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.690
Can martial arts really clear your Hue?

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:18.570
Of course.
A healthy mind dwells in a healthy body.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:24.370
I don't get it. It's just a way to beat up
people who piss you off, right?

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.370
You're an enforcer, aren't you?

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.210
What about it?

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.890
What a pitiful man you are!

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.390
Don't give up just because
you're a latent criminal!

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.230
Love yourself! Fight for it!

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:54.980
It's not too late for you! Live strong!

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.070
Mr. Yakushiji.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.650
What?

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.110
The two minutes we gave them are up.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.200
Oh, right!

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.200
Your car has arrived, sir.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.830
Do your best. Keep at it.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.710
What is it? You know him?

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.380
No.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.510
He is the shame of the Todoroki family.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.430
Please forget him.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.640
It sounds like there's a story there...

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.430
Well, I look forward to your support!

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:39.770
So, an enforcer has relatives
working on the Yakushiji campaign?

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.780
Dr. Tsuchiya specialized in neuroscience.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:53.160
Particularly, self-control via stereotypes
in the decision-making process.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.170
What does that mean?

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:01.460
One experiment with negative
and positive stereotypes

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.470
goes like this:

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:09.470
First, you take students of equal academic
ability and split them into two groups.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.600
You tell group A they're poor students

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.690
and tell group B they're
the advanced class.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:19.020
Then, you have them take a test.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:24.320
Even though they're intellectually equal,
there's a gap in their scores,

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.570
right?

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:29.320
Acting strong is all it takes
to make the human brain

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:34.540
secrete testosterone,
a hormone that encourages risk-taking.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.790
In contrast, acting weak

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.000
causes it to secrete
the stress-relief hormone cortisol.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.920
Huh. So, what's that got to do
with the accident?

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.590
Something, I hope.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:53.310
You seem pretty fixated
on this accident, Inspector.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:57.060
Are you following orders
from Chief Shimotsuki?

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.610
No, just my intuition.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.440
Intuition, huh?

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.200
Karina will be the next governor for sure.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:09.030
Yeah.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.910
I definitely hope she is.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.750
We need to Karina to keep
those people under control.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.830
I know.
Just looking at them clouds my Hue.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.050
Good afternoon, young ladies.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.590
Having English-style afternoon tea?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.680
Might I suggest coffee?

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.640
After all, English tea culture

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:39.890
only began because they lost a trade war.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:46.150
By the way, I'm the owner of this café.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:54.910
Case No. 10785, is it?

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.080
OK.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:05.090
First Inspector.
I will resume my duties as floorman.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:16.310
I know the world
is full of people in need.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.520
But I want to help my neighbors first.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.520
Those I can reach out and touch.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.360
That's the kind of government
I want to create.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:34.120
This speech is a live broadcast, isn't it?

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:35.450
Yeah, it's live.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:41.870
Direct appeals are more effective,
since they influence the citizens' Hues.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:47.420
The Neighbor Policy was formulated by the
Affirmation Party, which endorsed Komiya.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:53.640
They actually just want to regulate
immigrants and protect their interests.

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:57.890
You're sure politically minded, Irie.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.250
Inspector!

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:26.920
What happened?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.050
What is it? Is he sick?

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:30.960
Hello?

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:31.760
Doctor.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.550
Something's up with Inspector Shindo.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.760
Side effects of a Mental Trace.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.350
This is a serious case.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.020
Should we administer an anxiolytic?

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.070
No, he'll be fine.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.900
Hey, what are you doing?

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.700
Calling him back.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:03.370
But I want to help my neighbors first.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.210
Those I can reach out and touch.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:10.880
Arata.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:13.210
Arata!

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:18.800
Arata.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:27.520
Kei...

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:30.860
So, you're back, you idiot.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:34.240
You're quick to call me an idiot.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.570
You've been diving too much.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.200
You're under too much strain.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.830
Never mind me. Look into Karina Komiya.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.750
She's hiding something.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.300
I got unofficial complaints from
two gubernatorial candidates today alone.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:57.840
They were unofficial?

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.100
That's a relief.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:05.890
Internal Affairs sent us a warning
to stop interfering in the election.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.600
So, what did you find?

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.440
Any criminal activity?

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:13.360
As of now, the death seems accidental.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.490
What do you think you're doing?

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:23.280
Playing a game of "how close can we get
to getting Chief Shimotsuki fired"?

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:26.540
I wouldn't play that. It sounds boring.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.500
But say there's a risk of terrorism.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.290
That's a possibility?

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:37.510
Yes, ma'am. I believe a precautionary
investigation is permitted in that case.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:44.430
"We're not interfering in the election.
Just the opposite, in fact..."

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:52.650
That was a surprise. Was Dr. Tsuchiya's
research really that dangerous?

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.150
Well, I'm not sure.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.990
That's underhanded...

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.740
Chief Shimotsuki realizes that.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:05.160
Making it a precautionary anti-terror
investigation helps us deflect complaints.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.960
Is Karina Komiya hiding
something that critical?

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.840
I've never seen a mind like hers.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:18.340
It's thinking at frightening speeds,
but it's empty.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:22.050
Empty? She seems ambitious to me.

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:27.180
A mind like that could force someone
to weigh their Hue against their life

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:29.520
and make them choose death.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.520
Like the transport drone crash?

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:37.070
Or like our case.

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.570
If that's true...

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:46.530
Then she's connected
to the truth we're seeking.

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:53.330
I cross-referenced
the hotel's security data.

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:58.670
Now, pop quiz: What did I find?

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.960
Pop quiz?

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:03.010
That's too simple to be
a quiz question.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:08.010
Are you guys yanking my chain?

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.350
Just spit it out, Arata.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:17.270
Fine. A Yakushiji staffer was staying
at the hotel where Dr. Tsuchiya died.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:18.520
Correct.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:24.030
Kosuke Yakushiji's first secretary
Lee Aki was staying at the hotel.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:28.120
It's too much to be a coincidence.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.080
I guess this is the only lead we have.

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:35.830
Delivery complete.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.760
I was not aware
of Dr. Tsuchiya's presence.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.560
It was a coincidence.
I have nothing to hide.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:55.190
I can check that with a Dominator
if you like.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:57.560
Do as you wish. It won't help you.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:02.280
Mr. Lee, you tried to make contact
with Dr. Tsuchiya.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:07.780
But you couldn't, because the bodyguards
from the Komiya campaign stopped you.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:11.660
You wanted inside info
on an opposing candidate.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:17.170
You probably thought that Dr. Tsuchiya
was Karina Komiya's Achilles' heel.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:18.790
Nonsense.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.260
Please don't make me
draw my Dominator.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:25.430
I don't want to inconvenience the hotel.

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:28.260
I told you to point it at me if you like.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.260
I won't.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:35.810
Instead, let me ask this.
Does Mr. Yakushiji know

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.940
that you were in Dr. Tsuchiya's hotel?

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:44.610
Mr. Yakushiji doesn't bother
to check my every movement.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.610
I'll ask him, then.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.740
Please wait here.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.330
You have two minutes.

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.950
I'll make it quick.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.960
You seem awfully devoted
to Candidate Yakushiji.

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:06.220
Countless athletes have suffered setbacks,
despite having Sibyl suitability.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:12.720
Mr. Yakushiji is the only person
who genuinely supports people like them.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:19.350
I see. And he save you, too?

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:24.440
Yes, he did. No one is more qualified
to be Tokyo's leader.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.990
He's a hero born to be on top.

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:34.870
Area Stress Alert.
Perform psychological care immediately.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:51.590
Health check.
Your head has sustained a severe impact.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.680
There is a high probability
you are under assault.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.430
You don't say!

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.100
Evasive action recommended.

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:02.020
I would if I could, moron!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:20.120
Who are you people?

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.260
Crime Coefficient is 305.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.050
Lethal Eliminator.
Target for enforcement action.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:34.890
You gotta be kidding me!

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.270
What now?

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:40.180
Arrest them.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:42.900
Are you stupid?
Don't give me naïve crap.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.490
Temma, take the right.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.420
Where'd he learn that?

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:49.300
You're under arrest.

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:56.050
You let him get away? Come on.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:17:02.980
Why did you stop me?
The Dominator said to enforce them.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:07.730
We need to exercise human judgment.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:14.650
That's why the Dominator has a trigger.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.490
I repeat: We have breaking news.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:27.080
Gubernatorial candidate Kosuke Yakushiji's
first secretary,

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:31.500
Mr. Lee Aki was assaulted and
brutally murdered.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.680
The killers announced the crime online

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:40.100
and allegedly committed hate speech
against Mr. Lee Aki's ethnicity.

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:49.520
That's filthy! Azusawa, you scumbag!

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:54.400
Huh? What was that for?

00:17:55.780 --> 00:18:00.830
I wonder whose down card
attacked the Yakushiji campaign.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:05.960
Even if one of us stepped forward
and claimed responsibility,

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.420
would you believe us?

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:13.170
Invest in public-opinion-control AI bots.

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:16.880
Dealing with the Relation Block can wait.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:20.340
I also bet on public opinion control.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:24.680
I propose resetting the priority
of Public Safety Bureau

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:27.560
Criminal Investigation Department
Unit One.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:30.730
I object. The risk is too great.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:36.360
It could easily alert Sibyl
to our existence again.

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:38.360
I concur.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.910
In that case,
I will dispose of the assets.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.950
Oh, my. It must be tough being the dealer.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:52.080
If you fail to dispose of them, Roundrobin
will take enforcement action against you,

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:53.960
Understood, Shizuka?

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:00.970
If Kosuke Yakushiji
becomes governor of Tokyo,

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:04.220
foreigners will take our jobs
and our rights.

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:10.230
We must not allow
the pro-immigrant faction to destroy

00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.400
our peaceful society.

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:15.900
As I thought, online opinion

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:20.570
is pretty unanimous that Karina Komiya
supporters are behind it.

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:25.200
Both Yakushiji
and the Eugenics Party that endorsed him

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:28.250
welcome anti-isolation policies,
after all.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:31.710
To a thoroughbred like him,

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:35.250
race doesn't matter
as long as they have good genes.

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:39.260
And the corporate alliance behind them

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:43.720
only care about hiring hordes
of immigrants as cheap labor.

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.010
They're all pieces of crap.

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:51.520
What's the actual likelihood
that the Komiya campaign is behind it?

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:57.530
Well, Komiya's campaign manager
was an immigrant.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:01.530
She's been with Ms. Komiya
since she went independent.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:04.740
She might be breaking the party line.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:07.280
That's probably just a front.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:12.290
The Affirmation Party tacitly accepts
low-wage laborers too.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:17.130
Either way, the polls have flipped.
Yakushiji is the frontrunner.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.460
Komiya is at a disadvantage.

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:24.720
In the end, Inspector Shindo's prediction
was right on the money.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:26.430
What prediction?

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:28.470
About possible terrorism.

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:29.810
Good work.

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.640
I can't be happy about it.

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:37.110
People dying like that, whether
perpetrators or victims, is a tragedy.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:42.030
Whatever the reason may be.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.950
As for the man we arrested,
his background's a total blank.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:51.540
All assailants were from abandoned zones
and excluded from the census.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:55.790
Even if they moved through blind spots
in the street scanners,

00:20:56.080 --> 00:21:01.050
could latent criminals really operate
openly over such a wide area?

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:06.050
And breaking into a hotel?
That should be impossible.

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:10.560
But not only did they get in,
one of them got away.

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:12.810
It's clearly suspicious.

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:17.810
Yakushiji has three campaign offices.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:23.070
One in Ikebukuro, one in Suidobashi,
and one inside the Diet.

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:29.410
Even if they could dodge street scanners,
they wouldn't have risked discovery.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:35.370
If I were them, I'd build a base
as close as possible and form a plan.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.880
You can get easy access to two of those...

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:40.090
Myogadani

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:42.710
From Myogadani.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:48.930
Hey, wasn't the abandoned zone there
your old stomping grounds?

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:59.310
The assailants must have come from here.

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:01.480
They clearly practiced martial arts.

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:04.900
Yes, they were versed
in hand-to-hand combat.

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:07.990
That's unusual under the Sibyl System.

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.700
There's a place where it is usual.

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:12.700
Signal lost.

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:17.870
Relays are required for Dominator usage.
Proceed with caution.

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:20.500
Shut up. I know that.

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:26.090
Hey. Long time no see.

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:30.640
Irie.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:41.900
A human-on-human combat arena.

00:22:42.150 --> 00:22:47.240
If Yakushiji is the public champion,
that's the underground champion.

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:52.740
Broker of the abandoned zone,
Haruki Enomiya.

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:56.200
Ex-pro athlete, and an ex-woman.

00:22:56.700 --> 00:23:01.670
Retired in disgrace after overuse
of male hormones and body modifications.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:04.670
So, would they know Yakushiji?

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.170
I wouldn't be surprised.

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:10.680
Enomiya's Hue deteriorated
due to body changes and a poor record.

00:23:11.050 --> 00:23:15.600
And when they left center stage,
they built themselves a castle here.

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:17.520
Sounds like our culprit.

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:20.020
That's why I brought you here.

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:22.980
Thank you. I'm counting on you.

00:23:23.230 --> 00:23:24.320
Hey.

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:32.490
Enomiya gets athletes
with clouded Hues to fight here,

00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:36.490
taking bets on their matches
while raising strong soldiers.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:40.160
We've got a suspect.

00:23:40.370 --> 00:23:45.590
Now we just need a way to move fighters
without triggering street scanners.

00:23:46.210 --> 00:23:49.050
Then let's haul Enomiya in
for questioning.

00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:52.090
Whoa there, are you stupid?

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:54.140
Just look around.

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:58.850
They're the head of a huge organization.
What if they make a fuss?

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:02.270
We didn't come here to start a war.

00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:04.730
Yes, just to ask questions.

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:06.360
Very funny.

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:10.320
All right, Inspector,
I'll work something out.

00:24:13.780 --> 00:24:16.160
It's been a long time, Mr. Irie.

00:24:17.410 --> 00:24:20.160
Looks like you're doing well, Oishi.

00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:23.870
This is a one-time deal.

00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:26.880
I know. Thanks.

00:24:30.550 --> 00:24:33.840
I see you haven't changed.

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:46.980
Right this way.

00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:56.410
Voluntary questioning?

00:24:56.910 --> 00:24:57.700
Yes.

00:24:58.780 --> 00:25:00.200
Interesting.

00:25:01.120 --> 00:25:02.910
You've got promise.

00:25:03.410 --> 00:25:09.210
Are you unawhere of where you are,
or are you just that confident?

00:25:09.420 --> 00:25:11.420
Either way, you've got nerve.

00:25:11.840 --> 00:25:14.010
We're not idiots or overconfident.

00:25:14.130 --> 00:25:17.430
Questioning suspicious people
is a detective's job.

00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:22.430
Osamu, sit.

00:25:24.690 --> 00:25:26.560
Let me ask you a question, then.

00:25:29.650 --> 00:25:31.230
Do you recognize this face?

00:25:34.610 --> 00:25:39.320
As you can see, this place is free,
unlike the world outside.

00:25:39.580 --> 00:25:41.830
You can't expect me
to remember every face.

00:25:42.450 --> 00:25:45.080
I hear you raise fighters here.

00:25:45.290 --> 00:25:49.590
As merchandise.
But none of them can leave here.

00:25:50.130 --> 00:25:52.630
Just like ferocious animals in a zoo.

00:25:52.880 --> 00:25:56.180
But ferocious animals in zoos
are properly trained.

00:25:57.510 --> 00:25:58.340
Oishi.

00:26:02.970 --> 00:26:03.640
Yes, Boss.

00:26:04.480 --> 00:26:05.770
Open your mouth.

00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:07.100
Yes, Boss.

00:26:12.780 --> 00:26:13.610
Eat it.

00:26:14.320 --> 00:26:15.070
Yes, Boss.

00:26:22.330 --> 00:26:25.950
They're trained, just like circus animals.

00:26:26.660 --> 00:26:28.620
That's enough. Leave us.

00:26:33.340 --> 00:26:34.880
A circus, huh?

00:26:39.470 --> 00:26:43.430
I'm disappointed in you, Kazumichi Irie.

00:26:43.850 --> 00:26:46.350
You used to be the sharpest man we had.

00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:52.150
And yet you ended up a Public Safety dog.
I didn't even have to break you.

00:26:53.360 --> 00:26:55.650
Don't talk like you know me.

00:26:55.900 --> 00:26:58.820
What lout have you
been wagging your tail for?

00:27:02.070 --> 00:27:03.740
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:27:08.830 --> 00:27:12.420
I'm still as sharp as I ever was.

00:27:16.710 --> 00:27:19.340
Ouch, that hurts!

00:27:21.550 --> 00:27:23.930
What did you get all worked up for?

00:27:24.390 --> 00:27:25.680
Sorry.

00:27:28.390 --> 00:27:34.570
Enomiya's a likely suspect, but why
would they attack the Yakushiji campaign?

00:27:34.770 --> 00:27:36.360
Wouldn't it be for money?

00:27:36.650 --> 00:27:41.700
I doubt anyone could pay Enomiya
and keep their Hue clear.

00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:49.200
If the Sibyl System got serious, it could
stamp out the abandoned zones easily.

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:54.710
What would they stand to gain
that'd be worth that risk?

00:27:55.420 --> 00:27:59.380
Weren't these zones abandoned
because they'd be too hard to rebuild?

00:27:59.590 --> 00:28:01.300
They were left deliberately.

00:28:02.380 --> 00:28:07.720
To cut costs nation-wide and give people
outside them mental breathing room.

00:28:08.270 --> 00:28:11.140
A spontaneously-occurring safety net.

00:28:12.140 --> 00:28:17.730
Packaging complex systems of unforeseeable
crimes in isolated areas as slums

00:28:17.900 --> 00:28:19.740
made them easier to monitor.

00:28:21.490 --> 00:28:27.030
The abandoned zones themselves are
a part of psychological care, so to speak.

00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:33.000
This place isn't a garbage dump.

00:28:35.080 --> 00:28:37.000
Those bean sprouts were great.

00:28:37.500 --> 00:28:41.090
What was your impression, Arata?
Of Enomiya, I mean.

00:28:42.630 --> 00:28:46.760
A criminal. Not the mastermind,
so probably an accomplice.

00:28:47.050 --> 00:28:49.770
What's your basis for saying that?

00:28:50.100 --> 00:28:54.730
If someone asked you to come in
for questioning, you'd want to know why.

00:28:55.350 --> 00:28:58.520
But Enomiya
asked almost no questions.

00:28:59.150 --> 00:29:03.280
No "Why me?" or
"What am I suspected of?"

00:29:03.450 --> 00:29:05.530
Well, now that you mention it...

00:29:05.820 --> 00:29:07.700
There are three questions left.

00:29:08.410 --> 00:29:13.710
One, how did they send attackers into
an urban area and avoid street scanners?

00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:16.540
Two, what was in it for Enomiya?

00:29:17.750 --> 00:29:18.630
And the third?

00:29:19.090 --> 00:29:23.590
How was the ramen so delicious?
I still can't believe it.

00:29:23.840 --> 00:29:24.970
Don't ask me!

00:29:33.180 --> 00:29:35.810
Long time no see, Second Inspector.

00:29:36.100 --> 00:29:38.980
What's this about? You must be busy.

00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:42.530
Oh, don't play innocent.

00:29:43.150 --> 00:29:44.570
What was that attack?

00:29:45.070 --> 00:29:47.280
Part of the Relation.

00:29:47.530 --> 00:29:51.580
A congressman included me in their plans.

00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:53.750
I know that.

00:29:54.330 --> 00:29:57.830
I'm asking about your sloppy execution.

00:29:59.710 --> 00:30:02.840
I just imitated the First's methods.

00:30:03.380 --> 00:30:05.010
That was nothing like mine.

00:30:05.220 --> 00:30:08.720
I always ensure my target
finish themselves.

00:30:09.390 --> 00:30:14.350
What I do is art.
What you do is a half-baked copy.

00:30:14.680 --> 00:30:16.690
Are you getting anxious?

00:30:17.060 --> 00:30:21.400
Worried that I'll steal the rank of First
you worked so hard for?

00:30:22.820 --> 00:30:25.530
Hardly. I would never...

00:30:27.650 --> 00:30:28.950
Wait, that means...

00:30:30.450 --> 00:30:33.370
I see. That's what this is about.

00:30:37.910 --> 00:30:39.500
Hey, Azusawa.

00:30:40.420 --> 00:30:41.420
I've heard enough.

00:30:41.750 --> 00:30:44.800
I know how this incident will end.

00:30:45.550 --> 00:30:48.010
I'll start the clean-up. Bye.

00:30:56.060 --> 00:31:00.560
It seems you're advancing successfully.

00:31:00.770 --> 00:31:02.400
Yes, Father.

00:31:02.940 --> 00:31:08.400
As you should. I raised you to win.

00:31:08.950 --> 00:31:12.740
Discard any emotion that gets in your way.

00:31:13.330 --> 00:31:17.080
Win at any cost.

00:31:17.580 --> 00:31:19.410
If it helps you win,

00:31:19.620 --> 00:31:22.920
you should even use your own life.

00:31:24.210 --> 00:31:26.420
Yes, Father.

00:31:37.270 --> 00:31:38.100
Sir.

00:31:39.520 --> 00:31:40.480
Excuse me.

00:31:41.190 --> 00:31:44.150
This area is for the owner's personal use.

00:31:45.730 --> 00:31:47.280
I am the owner.

00:31:48.150 --> 00:31:50.200
No, I believe it's someone else...

00:31:50.320 --> 00:31:53.490
As of today, I'm the owner.
I invite you to confirm it.

00:32:02.370 --> 00:32:05.590
I will survive.

00:32:09.800 --> 00:32:12.510
Mrs. Maiko Maya Stronskaya,
please come in.

00:32:13.470 --> 00:32:18.270
An ordinary ocular prosthesis won't allow
your wife to regain her eyesight.

00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:24.650
With the latest surgical techniques,
however, success is highly likely.

00:32:25.270 --> 00:32:26.610
Thank you very much.

00:32:27.150 --> 00:32:32.030
We'll provide our best staff for the wife
of a Public Safety Bureau inspector.

00:32:32.950 --> 00:32:34.780
Sorry. I know you have work.

00:32:35.160 --> 00:32:37.580
Don't worry. I let Arata know.

00:32:37.700 --> 00:32:39.450
How long do I have to wait?

00:32:39.660 --> 00:32:42.620
Please, sir, wait your turn.

00:32:43.870 --> 00:32:46.960
Why did an immigrant get seen before me?!

00:32:48.380 --> 00:32:50.670
Not so loud. This is a hospital.

00:32:51.170 --> 00:32:52.970
Get out, foreigner!

00:32:57.010 --> 00:33:00.470
Public Safety Bureau.
I don't want to make matters worse.

00:33:01.850 --> 00:33:04.140
You work for the Public Safety Bureau?

00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:07.810
What's this country coming to?

00:33:09.230 --> 00:33:10.900
I won't accept it!

00:33:11.820 --> 00:33:14.740
I won't let you have this country!

00:33:19.620 --> 00:33:21.330
Sorry, I ran late.

00:33:21.580 --> 00:33:24.330
It's fine.
The briefing's just about to start.

00:33:24.870 --> 00:33:28.340
So, if we start by saying that Enomiya
is going rogue,

00:33:28.460 --> 00:33:31.090
we should get
the abandoned zone's cooperation.

00:33:31.380 --> 00:33:34.090
It's best if we reached
an amicable resolution.

00:33:34.380 --> 00:33:38.930
OK, Inspector. I'll get to gathering intel
around the abandoned zone.

00:33:39.050 --> 00:33:40.510
I'll go with him.

00:33:40.720 --> 00:33:42.180
I knew you'd say that.

00:33:43.480 --> 00:33:49.190
In that case, Todoroki and I
will investigate the victims.

00:33:49.480 --> 00:33:50.980
You don't mean...

00:33:51.320 --> 00:33:53.990
Yakushiji's election office and committee.

00:33:54.190 --> 00:33:57.030
No thanks. You know my reasons.

00:33:57.240 --> 00:34:00.030
There are things only family would notice.

00:34:00.240 --> 00:34:02.740
That's why I can't understand them.

00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:04.870
Obey your superior's orders!

00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:07.210
Understood.

00:34:13.130 --> 00:34:18.090
You should come at night next time.
We'll take care of that little boy, too.

00:34:22.060 --> 00:34:24.720
Everyone trusts you, huh, Irie?

00:34:24.980 --> 00:34:28.650
Well, I like the people here.

00:34:29.440 --> 00:34:33.020
A lot of them are hopeless,
but they're all full of life.

00:34:35.110 --> 00:34:36.650
I think so, too.

00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:44.330
You became an enforcer
to protect this place, didn't you?

00:34:46.120 --> 00:34:48.250
I never said...

00:34:52.130 --> 00:34:54.800
You're a weird inspector.

00:34:56.090 --> 00:34:58.260
Give it a rest!

00:34:59.470 --> 00:35:01.800
Who let them in here?

00:35:03.810 --> 00:35:06.180
Lee... I...

00:35:06.470 --> 00:35:07.930
We will arrest the...

00:35:08.100 --> 00:35:08.940
Silence!

00:35:09.140 --> 00:35:13.190
How insensitive must you be
to interview a man in his condition?

00:35:13.520 --> 00:35:15.440
Mr. Yakushiji is a victim!

00:35:20.110 --> 00:35:22.320
Let me be blunt, Temma.

00:35:22.950 --> 00:35:26.290
This is no place
for a latent criminal like you.

00:35:26.490 --> 00:35:28.540
We live in different worlds.

00:35:33.080 --> 00:35:36.920
How far must you drag
our family name through the mud?

00:35:37.670 --> 00:35:43.350
You must know all the slander
Father suffered because of you.

00:35:43.680 --> 00:35:45.560
You're just like my pathetic stepmother.

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:50.310
Since you inherited inferior genes,
I don't consider you my brother.

00:35:50.890 --> 00:35:52.440
Just a latent criminal.

00:35:53.480 --> 00:35:55.110
Just disappear like she...

00:36:01.280 --> 00:36:02.990
This is abuse of authority!

00:36:03.530 --> 00:36:05.450
I'll have you fired!

00:36:07.240 --> 00:36:10.290
You're suspended until the bureau chief
orders otherwise.

00:36:10.410 --> 00:36:13.750
Your Crime Coefficient and
inspector suitability will be reassessed.

00:36:14.630 --> 00:36:17.050
The final decision
will be made after that.

00:36:17.840 --> 00:36:18.760
Any questions?

00:36:20.170 --> 00:36:21.010
None, ma'am.

00:36:23.050 --> 00:36:24.510
Say, Inspector.

00:36:25.720 --> 00:36:26.510
What is it?

00:36:26.640 --> 00:36:29.180
Don't give me that.
What were you thinking?

00:36:30.730 --> 00:36:35.690
No causal link has been proven between
Crime Coefficient and blood relation.

00:36:37.400 --> 00:36:40.400
His remarks were not
in accordance with Sibyl.

00:36:48.450 --> 00:36:49.240
That said,

00:36:52.580 --> 00:36:53.920
I acted out of order.

00:36:55.130 --> 00:36:55.920
I'm sorry.

00:36:57.460 --> 00:37:01.970
I guess that wasn't very inspector-like.

00:37:02.970 --> 00:37:05.050
What? Suspended from duty?

00:37:09.470 --> 00:37:13.390
That airhead kid is going to investigate
the assault case alone?

00:37:13.690 --> 00:37:14.810
You must be joking.

00:37:15.100 --> 00:37:19.230
Those two are certainly good
at making messes bigger.

00:37:20.400 --> 00:37:26.570
If they're that concerned with accidents,
they might look into past inspectors'.

00:37:26.820 --> 00:37:29.280
Don't bring that up out of the blue.

00:37:29.740 --> 00:37:32.250
The chief already closed the case, right?

00:37:32.790 --> 00:37:37.750
If they investigate, we latent criminals
will just get roped in.

00:37:38.750 --> 00:37:41.000
More importantly, nerdy kid,

00:37:41.590 --> 00:37:43.840
aren't you done checking on them yet?

00:37:43.970 --> 00:37:48.220
Huh? I found the inspectors'
career data ages ago.

00:37:48.340 --> 00:37:50.560
Tell us that sooner, man.

00:37:51.850 --> 00:37:53.140
Let's see what we got.

00:37:53.680 --> 00:37:55.810
Arata Shindo, age 24.

00:37:56.310 --> 00:37:59.770
Special-A-class profiler
with high empathic abilities.

00:38:00.230 --> 00:38:04.610
Recommended for assignment by...
Akane Tsunemori?

00:38:05.110 --> 00:38:07.280
You mean the killer ex-inspector?

00:38:07.530 --> 00:38:10.120
Inspector Tsunemori is a great person.

00:38:10.370 --> 00:38:13.870
I heard she was a top-notch
inspector who lost her mind.

00:38:14.500 --> 00:38:18.170
His mother chose euthanasia due to illness
when he was young.

00:38:18.500 --> 00:38:19.880
His father killed himself.

00:38:20.380 --> 00:38:24.880
His father, Atsushi Shindo, was a former
top Ministry of Welfare official.

00:38:25.010 --> 00:38:26.800
Talk about a spoiled rich boy!

00:38:26.930 --> 00:38:30.010
Information on the suicide is restricted.

00:38:30.180 --> 00:38:33.470
It's level three classified.
I can't retrieve it.

00:38:33.720 --> 00:38:39.810
Anyway, after euthanasia and a suicide,
I'm amazed his Hue didn't cloud.

00:38:40.230 --> 00:38:42.820
Anything on Inspector Ignatov?

00:38:45.280 --> 00:38:48.490
24-year-old Russian
naturalized Japanese.

00:38:48.660 --> 00:38:53.950
Military training from his home country.
Excels in shooting, combat, and analysis.

00:38:54.080 --> 00:38:56.750
Recommended by Chief Shimotsuki.

00:38:57.830 --> 00:39:01.000
Wow. I didn't know
Inspector Ignatov was married.

00:39:02.540 --> 00:39:06.550
His wife is Maiko Maya Stronskaya, 24.

00:39:06.710 --> 00:39:10.050
She's visually impaired
and undergoing treatment.

00:39:10.390 --> 00:39:12.970
So he lives together with his blind wife?

00:39:13.810 --> 00:39:19.350
His brother, Akira Vasily Ignatov, was
also naturalized, but died two years ago.

00:39:20.440 --> 00:39:21.560
Was he murdered?!

00:39:22.230 --> 00:39:26.570
The suspect in Akira Vasily Ignatov's
murder was... Atsushi Shindo?

00:39:27.110 --> 00:39:32.820
So, Inspector Shindo's father killed
Inspector Ignatov's brother, then himself?

00:39:32.950 --> 00:39:35.200
What kinda relationship is this?

00:39:35.580 --> 00:39:39.580
The surviving family of a killer
and his victim became a buddy team?

00:39:40.080 --> 00:39:42.880
It's definitely pretty out there.

00:39:43.170 --> 00:39:45.420
There's a reason they stick together.

00:39:45.840 --> 00:39:48.880
The bond between them must be that strong.

00:39:49.090 --> 00:39:54.720
Having both lost family, they may have
had no choice but to trust each other.

00:39:54.890 --> 00:39:56.890
That's our Mao, always a romantic.

00:39:57.020 --> 00:39:59.310
Who said you could call me that?

00:40:00.310 --> 00:40:01.890
You're such a pig...

00:40:10.360 --> 00:40:15.740
Temma should have been born
with a genetically perfect Psycho-Pass.

00:40:16.580 --> 00:40:18.410
Are you saying it's my fault?

00:40:18.660 --> 00:40:21.120
Your deteriorating Hue proves it.

00:40:21.250 --> 00:40:23.080
Tokorozawa Correction Center

00:40:25.960 --> 00:40:28.920
Amazing how much difference
a mother makes.

00:40:30.170 --> 00:40:35.600
Great Sibyl assessments and gene editing,
but mother and son both latent criminals.

00:40:36.300 --> 00:40:37.100
Shut up.

00:40:38.390 --> 00:40:39.430
I'll cut to the chase.

00:40:40.980 --> 00:40:42.440
You see, Temma,

00:40:43.980 --> 00:40:46.150
your mother died last week.

00:40:47.940 --> 00:40:49.780
She took her own life.

00:40:50.320 --> 00:40:52.900
That saved me the trouble
of disposing of her.

00:41:02.160 --> 00:41:03.500
Gimme a break!

00:41:06.330 --> 00:41:08.880
What? You didn't tell Mai?

00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:10.170
That's awful.

00:41:10.340 --> 00:41:12.470
I planned to tell her later.

00:41:12.720 --> 00:41:15.050
What on Earth were you thinking?

00:41:15.340 --> 00:41:18.970
Striking a civilian? I can't believe it!

00:41:19.390 --> 00:41:22.520
He flew off the handle
when someone insulted his colleague.

00:41:23.020 --> 00:41:24.310
Kei's so kind.

00:41:24.730 --> 00:41:28.150
You always lose your cool
too quickly, dear.

00:41:28.650 --> 00:41:29.980
Think about what you did.

00:41:30.190 --> 00:41:30.900
I will.

00:41:31.820 --> 00:41:34.530
Wouldn't a food printer
be easier on you, Mai?

00:41:34.700 --> 00:41:36.700
What? After she cooked for you?

00:41:37.200 --> 00:41:39.660
The printer can't make
the food from my motherland.

00:41:40.410 --> 00:41:43.450
I don't want to forget the dishes
my mom taught me.

00:41:44.830 --> 00:41:45.920
That's true.

00:41:47.380 --> 00:41:50.800
Besides,
isn't it better than synthetic food?

00:41:52.300 --> 00:41:52.960
Yeah.

00:42:00.050 --> 00:42:01.720
Sorry for holding you back.

00:42:02.390 --> 00:42:03.850
Don't worry about it.

00:42:05.230 --> 00:42:10.150
Your Crime Coefficient and inspector-
suitability reevaluation were both clear.

00:42:10.820 --> 00:42:14.070
That means the Sibyl System understands.

00:42:15.700 --> 00:42:17.070
I hope so.

00:42:19.280 --> 00:42:20.620
Is the case going well?

00:42:21.160 --> 00:42:24.000
I'm missing a key piece of the puzzle.

00:42:25.500 --> 00:42:28.880
I'm pretty sure
Candidate Komiya is hiding it.

00:42:29.250 --> 00:42:31.880
Final Public Debate: Karina Komiya
vs. Kosuke "Heracles" Yakushiji

00:42:36.090 --> 00:42:38.130
What about security for the debate?

00:42:38.800 --> 00:42:40.550
Unit Two is handling it.

00:42:40.760 --> 00:42:41.760
I see.

00:42:44.720 --> 00:42:46.390
Getting enough sleep?

00:42:48.100 --> 00:42:49.400
Not sure.

00:42:49.560 --> 00:42:53.150
Your skill puts strain
on both your brain and mind.

00:42:53.650 --> 00:42:55.900
You shouldn't use it so frequently.

00:42:56.280 --> 00:42:59.530
If the investigation requires it,
I'll have to.

00:42:59.820 --> 00:43:02.070
Part of my job is not letting you.

00:43:02.490 --> 00:43:04.120
Aren't you suspended?

00:43:04.290 --> 00:43:06.250
I suppose I am.

00:43:08.040 --> 00:43:12.170
I'll do anything
if it means reaching the truth.

00:43:12.790 --> 00:43:15.130
You're not the only one.

00:43:17.050 --> 00:43:19.550
Just don't do it
when I can't hold your rope.

00:43:21.050 --> 00:43:23.100
I'm sorry about the other day.

00:43:24.310 --> 00:43:27.640
I can't see what you can.

00:43:28.680 --> 00:43:30.690
So at least let me back you up.

00:43:31.650 --> 00:43:33.520
Aren't you suspended?

00:43:34.070 --> 00:43:35.320
Drop it.

00:43:36.530 --> 00:43:38.280
I'll get reinstated soon.

00:43:41.820 --> 00:43:47.790
Why did Mai, you, and I
all have to lose family?

00:43:49.830 --> 00:43:51.960
We'll find out together.

00:44:08.470 --> 00:44:11.480
Stupid perfection in your own castle

00:44:13.650 --> 00:44:17.320
How smart. You cause me to yawn

00:44:18.730 --> 00:44:24.160
Look,
The key to the door is in your hand

00:44:24.320 --> 00:44:29.450
Don't you let anyone take control

00:44:29.580 --> 00:44:34.750
What do you want?

00:44:34.920 --> 00:44:40.130
Go get it. Play by your own rule

00:44:40.260 --> 00:44:46.010
The winner always controls the game

00:44:46.140 --> 00:44:50.980
You stand in your belief

00:44:54.350 --> 00:44:58.860
There's no promising future

00:44:59.320 --> 00:45:04.490
Always helpless
Crying for the moon

00:45:04.610 --> 00:45:09.700
Finger trembles in fear
With the weight of the trigger

00:45:09.870 --> 00:45:12.870
There's a way for us

00:45:13.040 --> 00:45:17.040
Show them how we fight

00:45:17.210 --> 00:45:20.210
Pull the trigger

00:45:25.800 --> 00:45:28.390
To fill the gap left by Inspector Ignatov,

00:45:29.180 --> 00:45:33.980
I've asked an investigation consultant
contracted with the bureau to join us.

00:45:35.100 --> 00:45:36.400
Let me introduce her.

00:45:36.770 --> 00:45:40.400
Former Unit One enforcer
and current freelance journalist,

00:45:41.440 --> 00:45:43.070
Yayoi Kunizuka.

00:45:45.400 --> 00:45:47.450
"Psycho-Pass" refers to the measurement
of a person's mind and personality.

00:45:47.570 --> 00:45:49.700
This is a work of fiction. Any resemblance
to real persons or groups is coincidental.
